# Cross compilation of QNX

1. Register yourself with qnx.com
1. Setup the license and get the details. Add QNX Software Development Platform 8.0 - Perpetual - Developer License - Non-Commercial Single-User License (Non-Commercial/Academic License Class) (ver. 8.0)
1. Add License key

```sh
~ qlicense -userEmail your@email.com -activateLicenseKey XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX
License key is added: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX
Info: Remote license activation is not required for this key

~ qlicense -listLicenseKeys
[XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX] - Activated - QNX Software Development Platform 8.0 Education
```

1. Download the SDP and extract it to `/path/qnx/sdp/`

1. Source the sdp and compile it using Makefile

```sh
. ~/qnx800/qnxsdp-env.sh
QNX_HOST=~/qnx800~/host/linux/x86_64
QNX_TARGET=~/qnx800/target/qnx
MAKEFLAGS=-I~/qnx800/target/qnx/usr/include

make
qcc -Vgcc_ntoaarch64le -c -Wp,-MMD,build/aarch64le-debug/src/HelloQnx.d,-MT,build/aarch64le-debug/src/HelloQnx.o -o build/aarch64le-debug/src/HelloQnx.o  -Wall -fmessage-length=0 -g -O0 -fno-builtin  src/HelloQnx.c
qcc -Vgcc_ntoaarch64le -o build/aarch64le-debug/HelloQnx   build/aarch64le-debug/src/HelloQnx.o


file build/aarch64le-debug/HelloQnx
build/aarch64le-debug/HelloQnx: ELF 64-bit LSB pie executable, ARM aarch64, version 1 (SYSV), dynamically linked, interpreter /usr/lib/ldqnx-64.so.2, BuildID[md5/uuid]=5301bc68758143560905d3a7441dd253, with debug_info, not stripped
```

1. Compile using CMake

Source the QNX SDP environment, configure CMake with the QNX toolchain, and
build the executable:

```sh
. ~/qnx800/qnxsdp-env.sh

cmake -S . -B build/cmake-aarch64le-debug -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=cmake/qnx-toolchain.cmake -DQNX_ARCH=aarch64le -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build build/cmake-aarch64le-debug

file build/cmake-aarch64le-debug/HelloQnx
```

To build for another QNX architecture, set `QNX_ARCH` to the corresponding
processor name, such as `x86_64`.
